=== foundation.dle first 100 lines ===
# DLe — Description Logic (Extended)
# This document uses standard Description Logic (DL) syntax for ontology axioms, with the following extensions:
#
# Annotations (lines beginning with @):
# @label <IRI> "text"  — display name of the resource
# @doc <IRI> "text"  — description of the resource
# @db <IRI>  — resource appears explicitly in the database using its own identifier
# @db <IRI> "identifier"  — resource appears explicitly in the database and is queried using this identifier
# @storage <IRI> "text"  — describes database storage details
# @ann <IRI> <annotation-property> "text"  — annotation using the given property
# @prefix <prefix>: <namespace>  — declares a prefix
# @import <IRI>  — imports another ontology
# @ontology <IRI>  — declares the ontology IRI
#
# Naming conventions:
# - Every entity has an implicit label equal to its identifier unless @label is declared
# - Unprefixed names (e.g., Application) are in the default namespace (:Application)
# - Prefixed names use declared prefixes (e.g., xsd:string)
# - Concept/class identifiers conventionally begin with an upper-case letter
# - Role/reference/field identifiers conventionally begin with a lower-case letter
#
# Database convention:
# - Resources only appear explicitly in the database if they have an @db annotation
#
# DLe extensions:
# ≝  — defines a symbol or predicate; right-hand side is not DL and is not required to be valid OWL
# ∃r₁,…,rₙ.P  — predicate restriction: P(r₁,…,rₙ) holds over the role values

@import "metaschema.dle"

ApplicationsWorkspace ⊑ Workspace
BusinessCapabilitiesWorkspace ⊑ Workspace
OrganizationWorkspace ⊑ Workspace
PeopleWorkspace ⊑ Workspace
@label ApplicationsWorkspace "Applications Workspace"
@label BusinessCapabilitiesWorkspace "Business Capabilities Workspace"
@label OrganizationWorkspace "Organization Workspace"
@label PeopleWorkspace "People Workspace"
@doc ApplicationsWorkspace "Workspace for application portfolio modeling."
@doc BusinessCapabilitiesWorkspace "Workspace for business capability modeling (capability maps / hierarchies)."
@doc OrganizationWorkspace "Workspace for modeling organizational structure (organizations and organizational units)."
@doc PeopleWorkspace "Workspace for modeling people and their roles/responsibilities (supports surveys/notifications)."

Application ⊑ Component
Application ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.ApplicationsWorkspace
@db Application

BusinessCapability ⊑ Component
BusinessCapability ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.BusinessCapabilitiesWorkspace
@label BusinessCapability "Business Capability"
@doc BusinessCapability "Represents what an organization does; typically modeled as a hierarchical capability map."
@db BusinessCapability

Organization ⊑ Component
Organization ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.OrganizationWorkspace

@doc Organization "Represents an organization or enterprise; may contain organizational units or sub-organizations."
@db Organization

OrganizationalUnit ⊑ Component
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.OrganizationWorkspace
@label OrganizationalUnit "Organizational Unit"
@doc OrganizationalUnit "Subdivision of an organization (e.g., department/team); may be related via hierarchy or belongsTo links."
@db OrganizationalUnit

Person ⊑ Component
Person ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.PeopleWorkspace
@doc Person "Named individual represented in the model, typically linked to other components via roles or responsibilities."
@db Person

BelongingEntity ⊑ Component
BelongingContainer ⊑ Component
@label BelongingEntity "Belonging Entity"
@label BelongingContainer "Belonging Container"
@doc BelongingEntity "An entity eligible to be the source of a belongsTo reference. Foundation identifies Person and OrganizationalUnit as known belonging entities; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."
@doc BelongingContainer "An entity eligible to be the target of a belongsTo reference. Foundation identifies Organization and OrganizationalUnit as known belonging containers; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."

Person ⊑ BelongingEntity
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ BelongingEntity
Organization ⊑ BelongingContainer
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ BelongingContainer

belongsTo ⊑ reference
∃belongsTo.⊤ ⊑ BelongingEntity
⊤ ⊑ ∀belongsTo.BelongingContainer
@db belongsTo "Belongs To"
@label belongsTo "Belongs To"
@doc belongsTo "Relates a BelongingEntity to a BelongingContainer. In Foundation, a Person belongs to an OrganizationalUnit, while an OrganizationalUnit may belong to an Organization or another OrganizationalUnit. OrganizationalUnit relationships are used for non-hierarchical organizational structures; hierarchical structures use parent."

Person ⊑ ∀belongsTo.OrganizationalUnit
OrganizationalUnit ⊑ ∀belongsTo.(Organization ⊔ OrganizationalUnit)

ConsumingEntity ⊑ Component
ConsumableEntity ⊑ Component
@label ConsumingEntity "Consuming Entity"
@label ConsumableEntity "Consumable Entity"
@doc ConsumingEntity "An entity eligible to be the source of a consumes reference. Foundation identifies OrganizationalUnit as a known consuming entity; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."
@doc ConsumableEntity "An entity eligible to be the target of a consumes reference. Foundation identifies Application as a known consumable entity; extending ontologies may declare additional subclasses."

OrganizationalUnit ⊑ ConsumingEntity
=== metaschema.dle ===
Workspace ⊑ ⊤
@doc Workspace "Container grouping components, primarily used for permissions and access control."
@db Workspace

Component ⊑ ⊤
Component ≡ (∃rootWorkspace.Workspace) ⊓ (∃name.xsd:string) ⊓ (=1 id.xsd:string)
@doc Component "Root node type for modeled graph entities. In Ardoq storage, the schema-level definition is called a ComponentType and each corresponding data record is called a Component; this ontology represents both through ordinary class membership."

Component ⊑ ¬Workspace

∃description.⊤ ⊑ Component
⊤ ⊑ ∀description.xsd:string
≤1 description.⊤
@db description
@label description "Description"
@doc description "Concise description of a component."

∃name.⊤ ⊑ Component
⊤ ⊑ ∀name.xsd:string
Component ⊑ ∃name.xsd:string
≤1 name.⊤
@db name
@label name "Name"
@doc name "Human-readable name of a component, unique within a workspace."

# `matches` references the OWL xsd:pattern facet. `key()` references owl:hasKey
∃id.⊤ ⊑ Component
⊤ ⊑ ∀id.[xsd:string ⊓ [matches("[0-9a-f]{24}")]]
Component ⊑ key(id)
@db id
@storage id "tinkerpop.T.id"
@doc id "Opaque unique identifier"

∃reference.⊤ ⊑ Component ⨆ Workspace
⊤ ⊑ ∀reference.(Component ⨆ Workspace)
@label reference "Reference"
@doc reference "Generic relationship between components or between components and workspaces, specialized by domain-specific subproperties. Ardoq stores the relationship definition as a ReferenceType and each use as a Reference; this ontology represents them as an RDF property and its asserted triples."

∃field.⊤ ⊑ Component ⊔ ReferenceDescription
⊤ ⊑ ∀field.(xsd:boolean ⊔ xsd:integer ⊔ xsd:decimal ⊔ xsd:string ⊔ xsd:dateTime ⊔ xsd:date)
@doc field "A scalar attribute belonging to a Component or to an asserted reference."

# ReferenceStatement is reserved for propositions whose corresponding reference triple is asserted in the model.
# This assertedness is an application invariant and is not entailed by rdf:reifies or by class membership alone.
# RDF 1.2 uses rdfs:Proposition as the class of propositions denoted by triple terms.

ReferenceStatement ⊑ rdfs:Proposition
@doc ReferenceStatement "A specialization of rdfs:Proposition whose described triple is asserted. The predicate of the triple is a reference type."
ReferenceDescription ⊑ ⊤
@doc ReferenceDescription "A resource that reifies a ReferenceStatement and carries fields or metadata about that reference. It provides an ordinary RDF subject because RDF 1.2 triple terms can occur only in object position. Used when attaching fields or metadata to a reference use."
describes ⊑ rdf:reifies
∃describes.⊤ ⊑ ReferenceDescription
⊤ ⊑ ∀describes.ReferenceStatement
@doc describes "A property that associates a ReferenceDescription with a ReferenceStatement (which is a proposition that is asserted)"
∃hasReference.⊤ ⊑ ReferenceDescription
⊤ ⊑ ∀hasReference.rdf:Property
@doc hasReference "The predicate of the reference proposition described by this ReferenceDescription. Its value is defined as matching the predicate of the triple term reified by `describes`."

## Fields that belong to a particular use of a reference are attached to a ReferenceDescription.
##
## hasReference identifies which reference type is being described.
## It is maintained by the data-conversion layer because RDF and OWL cannot derive it from the reified proposition.
##
## Example instance data:
##   :r :describes << :componentA :replaces :componentB >> .  # The proposition is therefore treated as a ReferenceStatement by Ardoq convention, because the conversion layer only creates ReferenceDescriptions for asserted reference triples.
##   :r :hasReference :replaces .  # the conversion layer defines this to match the predicate of the triple reified by :describes.
##   :r :startingAt "2027-01-01T00:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .  # the assertion of the field on the use of :replaces in the above triple term.
##
## Every reference type that has fields should define a corresponding subclass of ReferenceDescription constrained by hasReference.
## For example, an ontology may define:
# ReplacesDescription ⊑ ReferenceDescription ⊓ ∃hasReference.{replaces}
# ∃startingAt.⊤ ⊑ ReplacesDescription
# ⊤ ⊑ ∀startingAt.xsd:dateTime
#
## DLe annotations can associate these entities with labels and database identifiers:
# @label startingAt "Starting At"
# @db startingAt "starting_at"

calculatedValue ⊑ field
@label calculatedValue "Calculated"
@doc calculatedValue "Subproperties of this are system-calculated values; this property is not intended for direct use."

calculatedNumber ⊑ calculatedValue
⊤ ⊑ ∀calculatedNumber.(xsd:integer ⊔ xsd:decimal)
@label calculatedNumber "Calculated Number"
@doc calculatedNumber "Subproperties of this are numeric calculated values; this property is not intended for direct use."

calculatedList ⊑ calculatedValue
⊤ ⊑ ∀calculatedList.xsd:string
@doc calculatedList "Subproperties of this are calculated string values selected from a model-defined list of enumerated terms."

∃parent.⊤ ⊑ Component
⊤ ⊑ ∀parent.Component
≤1 parent.⊤
@db parent "ardoq_parent"
@label parent "Parent"
@doc parent "The stored Ardoq structural parent relation between components, intended as instance-level parent/child; do not assume rdfs:subClassOf semantics unless separately axiomatized."

# “ancestor” and “descendant” are conceptually transitive closures.
parent ⊑ ancestor
hasChild ≡ parent⁻
Trans(ancestor)
descendant ≡ ancestor⁻
hasChild ⊑ descendant

∃rootWorkspace.⊤ ⊑ Component
⊤ ⊑ ∀rootWorkspace.Workspace
@db rootWorkspace
@label rootWorkspace "Root Workspace"
@doc rootWorkspace "Primary workspace associated with a component."

